## Quick start

```bash
yarn install
cp .env.example .env   # fill in values
yarn start             # Expo dev client
```

First native run (generates `ios/` and `android/`):

```bash
npx expo prebuild
yarn ios               # or: yarn android
```

> `ios/` and `android/` are git-ignored and regenerated from `app.config.ts`. Configure native settings there, not in the native folders. Restart Metro with `npx expo start --clear` after `.env` changes.
<% if (hasAuth) { %>
Auth is optional at boot: the app runs without Supabase env vars (sign-in is disabled until `EXPO_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL` and `EXPO_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_KEY` are set).
<% } %>
## Scripts

| Command | Description |
|---------|-------------|
| `yarn start` | Expo dev server (dev client) |
| `yarn ios` / `yarn android` | Build & run on a simulator/device |
| `yarn lint` | Prettier check + TypeScript |
| `yarn test` | Jest |
| `yarn build:dev` / `build:preview` / `build:prod` | EAS builds |
| `yarn update:preview` / `update:production` | EAS OTA updates |

